From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:41:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: join the async pipeline workers before releasing the
 compiler

MESA_KK_ASYNC_PIPELINES builds a graphics pipeline's Metal render pipeline
state on a worker (0041).  kk_DestroyDevice released the device's Metal
compiler (kk_release_compiler) and only afterwards joined the workers in
util_queue_destroy.  vkDestroyPipeline waits for its program's job, but a
pipeline still alive at vkDestroyDevice keeps its job queued or running,
and a worker inside newRenderPipelineStateWithDescriptor then used the freed
MTL4 compiler: SIGSEGV or a pointer-authentication fault in AGXMetal's
compileProgram / populateRenderPipelineDescriptorInfo, with the main thread
in util_queue_destroy's thrd_join.

Destroy the queue first in kk_DestroyDevice, before anything a worker uses
is released.  Running jobs finish, queued ones are dropped with their
fences signalled, so a later kk_shader_destroy returns from
util_queue_drop_job without touching the destroyed queue.  No cost outside
device destruction, and none when async pipelines are off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c
index ff91cc3..a3a7798 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_device.c
@@ -478,6 +478,16 @@ kk_DestroyDevice(VkDevice _device, const VkAllocationCallbacks *pAllocator)
 
    kk_device_note_lifecycle(dev, false);
 
+   /* MESA_KK_ASYNC_PIPELINES: a worker may still be building the render
+    * pipeline state of a pipeline that is alive at device destruction (the
+    * application, or a guest context being torn down, did not destroy it).
+    * The worker compiles through dev->mtl_compiler_handle, so join the
+    * workers before anything they use is released. util_queue_destroy
+    * signals the fences of jobs no worker picked up, so a later
+    * kk_shader_destroy of such a program does not touch the queue. */
+   if (dev->async_pipelines)
+      util_queue_destroy(&dev->pipeline_queue);
+
    /* End capture before we start releasing resources. Otherwise, Metal capture
     * may run into issues. */
    if (pdev->settings.gpu_capture_enabled) {
@@ -506,11 +516,6 @@ kk_DestroyDevice(VkDevice _device, const VkAllocationCallbacks *pAllocator)
    kk_release_compiler(dev);
    simple_mtx_destroy(&dev->lazy_pipeline_lock);
 
-   /* Every shader is destroyed before vk_device_finish releases the pipeline
-    * cache (and its objects), so no async pipeline job can be in flight. */
-   if (dev->async_pipelines)
-      util_queue_destroy(&dev->pipeline_queue);
-
    vk_device_finish(&dev->vk);
 
    vk_free(&dev->vk.alloc, dev);
